CIX MVX: preserve single-planar DMA-BUF capture descriptors

MVX firmware may return an encoded bitstream at a non-zero offset within a
capture buffer. Multi-planar V4L2 represents this with data_offset, but the
single-planar DMA-BUF ABI has only a file descriptor and cannot communicate
the offset separately.

The dequeue path also switched on the buffer type instead of the memory
type. For capture type 1 this treated a DMA-BUF file descriptor as an MMAP
offset, corrupting the descriptor before it was returned and making requeue
fail.

Select the adjustment by memory type. For single-planar DMA-BUF capture,
compact a non-zero-offset payload while holding the exporter CPU-access
contract. Imported DMA-BUFs deliberately skip vb2 memops cache maintenance,
so bracket both the CPU read and write with the DMA-BUF exporter's begin/end
callbacks. This preserves the descriptor, cache coherency, and the existing
userspace ABI. Invalid, unmappable, or unsynchronisable payloads are returned
as errored, empty buffers instead of exposing unusable or stale data.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
@@ -34,7 +34,9 @@
